      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zeba%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The name Zeba means \"river\" in Ojibwa, named for a small stream southeast of the community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zeba%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Gothic-style Zeba Indian United Methodist Church, built in 1888, sits on a bluff overlooking the lake and is on the National Register.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zeba%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Zeba is part of the Keweenaw Bay Indian Community of the Lake Superior Band of Chippewa Indians.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
